// `html_escape` — the five entities, spelled the way the implementation people port FROM spells them.
//
// **This function had no test at all until 2026-08-21**, which is how a byte-level choice inside it
// went unexamined: `'` was written `&#39;` and Python's `html.escape` writes `&#x27;`. Both are
// correct HTML and they render identically, so nothing a reader looks at would ever show the
// difference — it shows up as a diff in a committed page, later, in a screenshot.
//
// The BMX session hit exactly that porting a Python generator: calling this library would have
// changed every page holding an apostrophe, so they wrote the table out by hand instead. That is a
// library being avoided for a reason that is one byte wide.
//
// Changed to hex after measuring that it churned nothing — no generated artefact in this repository
// or in star-burxt held either spelling from this function. **A byte-level choice is free to change
// only while nothing has committed its output**, and this test is what closes that window: the
// independent half, `html_escape_agrees_with_pythons_reference_escaper` in `tests/runner.rs`, hands
// this same text to `html.escape` and requires the bytes to match.
//
// The five and ONLY the five: anything else escaped here would be a second difference from every
// other escaper, and anything missing is an injection.
use "../../lib/html.bx";

region r {
    print(html_escape("it's a <b>\"test\"</b> & co"));
    // Each entity alone, so a failure names which one moved rather than "the string differs".
    print(html_escape("&"));
    print(html_escape("<"));
    print(html_escape(">"));
    print(html_escape("\""));
    print(html_escape("'"));
    // A byte that must NOT be escaped: the five are the whole list, and a sixth would diverge
    // from every other escaper in the world.
    print(html_escape("/"));
    // Runs matter: the implementation copies whole slices between entities, and an off-by-one
    // there loses text rather than mis-escaping it.
    print(html_escape("aaa'bbb'ccc"));
    print(html_escape("''"));
    print(html_escape(""));
}
